<title>BELGIUM: Forced EMU entry unlikely - Dutch minister Zalm.</title>
<headline>Forced EMU entry unlikely - Dutch minister Zalm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm said on Wednesday that it was very unlikely that a country would be forced to join the EU's economic and monetary union against its will.</p>
<p>Asked about Sweden's position that it is the national parliament that will decide whether the country should join EMU, Zalm told reporters that it was a legal debate.</p>
<p>&quot;I leave that to the lawyers. But it is very improbable that a country would be forced against its will to enter monetary union,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The issue is sensitive as Sweden insists that it will decide in the autumn on whether to join a single currency. But many argue that it is not in the same position as Britain and Denmark, both of which have negotiated the option of staying outside monetary union.</p>
</text>
